# Stow ignore list (blacklist) — GNU Stow >= 2.2
#
# Stow reads this file only at the root of the package being stowed, so it
# applies when the whole repository is the package:
#
#     stow -t ~ .
#
# scripts/stow/stow.sh reads the same file to skip blacklisted packages when
# each top-level directory is stowed on its own.
#
# Syntax: one Perl regex per line, "#" starts a comment. A pattern without "/"
# is matched against every path segment (at any depth); a pattern with "/" is
# matched against the path relative to the package root. Providing this file
# replaces stow's built-in defaults, so the defaults worth keeping are
# repeated at the bottom.

# --- NixOS: system configuration built with nixos-rebuild, never a dotfile
nixos

# --- repository tooling, not a dotfile package
scripts

# --- system files: they belong in /etc (sudo stow -t /etc etc)
etc

# --- leftovers from the old zsh layout
zsh.old

# --- documentation: it is read in the browser, not linked into $HOME
wiki

# --- the task list, for the same reason
^/TODO\.md$

# --- written by the noctalia theme template on every theme change: it is
# --- machine state, not a dotfile. The pattern is not anchored so it matches
# --- the path inside the "niri" package (.config/niri/noctalia.kdl) and the
# --- path inside the repository (niri/.config/niri/noctalia.kdl), while
# --- leaving the hand written theme/noctalia.kdl alone
/\.config/niri/noctalia\.kdl$

# --- stow defaults, repeated because this file replaces them
RCS
CVS
\.#.+       # CVS conflict files / emacs lock files
\.cvsignore
\.svn
_darcs
\.hg
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
.+~          # emacs backup files
\#.*\#       # emacs autosave files
